
# Path Fixtures in Lappa

## Coordinate Units

All path fixtures in Lappa are defined using meters as the unit of measurement. This ensures that the coordinates are consistent and easy to interpret across different simulations.

## Origin Conventions

The origin of the coordinate system is located at the bottom-left corner of the simulation environment. This convention helps in standardizing the placement and movement of robots within the simulation.

### Example Path Fixture

```json
{
  "waypoints": [
    {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.0},
    {"x": 1.5, "y": 8.0},
    {"x": 1.5, "y": 0.0},
    {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.0}
  ]
}
```

In this example, the robot starts at the origin `(0.0, 0.0)`, drives up the aisle to `(0.0, 8.0)`, strafes across to `(1.5, 8.0)`, drives back down to `(1.5, 0.0)`, and finally strafes back to the start `(0.0, 0.0)`.

## Usage

When defining path fixtures, ensure that the coordinates are in meters and follow the origin convention described above. This will help in maintaining consistency and making the simulations more interpretable.

